  <title>Pay stub</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Payroll</gui><gui>Manage payments</gui></guiseq> pays
  employees for the time punched in the <link xref="time_clock"/> and not yet
  paid, using what is kept in <link xref="employee_info"/>.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Pay Period ending</gui> date. The employees with
    unpaid time up to that date are listed under <gui>Employee</gui>, with
    <gui>Print All</gui> to do every one in turn.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the bank account the checks are drawn on. The next check
    number is filled in.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Step #1 Credit Dividends and Deductions</gui> to enter
    any extra pay or deductions for the employee: add a row for each, choose
    its <gui>Type</gui>, and type the <gui>Description</gui> and
    <gui>Amount</gui>. Check <gui>View Paid Entries</gui> to see ones already
    paid. Click <gui>Save</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>View Trial</gui> to print the time sheet and check it
    before paying.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Pay &amp; Close</gui>. The pay check prints and the
    pay is posted.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>The check template has room for only 10 lines each of dividends,
  deductions and cash advance payments.</p>

  <note><p>This window is not finished. <gui>Cash Advance</gui> does nothing
  yet, the items of the <gui>File</gui> and <gui>Edit</gui> menus do nothing,
  and the pay is posted even if the print dialog is cancelled.</p></note>

</page>
